  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we cancel any terms that appear in both a numerator and a denominator. Then, we multiply the numerators and the denominators as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{4{z}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{8xz}{y} & =\\frac{5y\\cdot y}{4z\\cdot z}\\cdot \\frac{4z\\cdot 2x}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{5y\\cdot \\cancel{y}}{\\cancel{4z}\\cdot z}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{4z}\\cdot 2x}{\\cancel{y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5y}{z}\\cdot \\frac{2x}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10xy}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
